  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 100 PM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nThrough the remainder of the week, the upper level ridge will\ncontinue building over the region, leading to mid-level heights\nrising and mostly clear skies. The NBM interquartile spread for\ntemperatures only shows a 2-4 degree difference between the \n25th and 75th percentiles, leading to high confidence in above \nnormal temperatures, with afternoon highs in the upper 70s and \neven reaching 80 in some locations through this weekend and into\nearly next week. Southerly surface winds should remain fairly \nlight, so any fire weather concerns remain limited. \n\nLots of model variances exist as we look ahead towards midweek\nnext week, with some showing a shortwave trough bringing\nprecipitation chances to the area once again, and others keeping\nthe rain out of the forecast area. Additionally, NBM\ninterquartile spreads increase to a 10-15 degree difference\n(ranging from the low 60s to upper 70s), leading to low \nconfidence in afternoon temperatures. With this being about a\nweek out, several variables will need to come into better \nagreement before confidence increases in the forecast.",
